Enable the SARADC.

The driver is built in and the rk3576 saradc node exists upstream, but
it is status disabled and the board dts never enables it, so /sys/bus/iio
stays empty. Enable it with the vref rail the vendor dts uses. The 40-pin
header exposes ADC inputs.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah Peng <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-sige5.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-sige5.dts
@@ -1087,3 +1087,12 @@
 	regulator-min-microvolt = <800000>;
 	regulator-max-microvolt = <800000>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * SARADC: upstream leaves it disabled and no in-tree board enables it.
+ * The 40-pin header exposes ADC inputs; vref wiring per the vendor dts.
+ */
+&saradc {
+	status = "okay";
+	vref-supply = <&vcca_1v8_s0>;
+};
